<title>GERMANY: German Oct/March sugar sales down from last year.</title>
<headline>German Oct/March sugar sales down from last year.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sugar sales in the first six months of the 1996/97 (Oct/Sept) season totalled 1.33 million tonnes, rounded, below the 1.35 million recorded in Oct/March 95/96, sugar industry association WVZ data showed.</p>
<p>Sugar sales in March of 209,406 tonnes compared with 224,985 in March 1996. Sugar production in March was 1,729 tonnes (1,804).</p>
<p>Stocks at the end of March were 2.30 million tonnes versus 1.99 million a year earlier. Carry-in stocks on Oct 1, 1996 were 239,562 tonnes (250,854) a year earlier).</p>
<p>March imports of 6,330 tonnes were slightly down from 6,391 tonnes a year earlier while exports of 92,729 tonnes compared with 89,546 in March 1996.</p>
<p>Cumulative details (in tonnes) --</p>
<p>					 Oct/March 96/97  Oct/March 95/96</p>
<p> Domestic sugar output	     4,182,466	3,808,940</p>
<p> Imports				    39,383	   59,650</p>
<p> Exports				   828,639	  783,092</p>
<p> Domestic sales			1,332,865	1,346,063</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
